-/**
- * NEWTUBE(startup): the baseline profile where ART itself looks for it at INSTALL time.
- *
- * AGP packages the profile as assets/dexopt/baseline.prof, which only androidx.profileinstaller
- * reads - on the app's first run it queues the profile for the next BACKGROUND dexopt (idle +
- * charging). NewTube is sideloaded (GitHub APK, in-app updater -> system installer), so an update
- * installs with filter "verify" and every cold start runs interpreted/JIT until that background
- * job: measured on the Pixel 9, cold share-link opens at median 926 ms right after install vs
- * 582 ms once compiled. Since Android 15, ART Service's install-time dexopt also reads an
- * EMBEDDED profile at assets/art-profile/baseline.prof (art/artd: kEmbeddedProfileEntry, used
- * when the APK comes without a .dm file) and compiles it right away. That entry must be a binary
- * profile in ART's own format (v0.1.5) keyed to the final dex, so it is generated here from the
- * merged dex and AGP's merged human-readable profile, and added as an ordinary asset (packaging
- * and signing are untouched). If profgen (cmdline-tools) is missing the task logs and emits
- * nothing; the APK is then exactly what it was before.
- */
-abstract class EmbeddedArtProfileTask extends DefaultTask {
-    @InputFiles
-    @PathSensitive(PathSensitivity.NAME_ONLY)
-    abstract ConfigurableFileCollection getDexFiles()
